<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marduk-zakir-shumi I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 855–819 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century-bce">9th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marduk-zakir-shumi I was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a> from about 855 to 819 BCE. When his brother Marduk-bel-usate revolted, he called on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shalmaneser-iii">Shalmaneser III</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a>, who defeated the rebel in 850 BCE; the two kings are shown clasping hands on a throne base from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nimrud">Nimrud</a>. He later supported Shamshi-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hadad">Adad</a> V of Assyria in his own succession war, and a treaty between the two survives.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marduk-zakir-shumi-i.jpg" alt="Marduk-zakir-shumi I" width="320" height="631" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Osama Shukir Muhammed Amin FRCP(Glasg) · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marduk-zakir-shumi_I.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
